{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The word of YHWH came to Abram in a vision</b> — Abraham now merited that the word of YHWH should come to him in a vision by day, for at first his prophecy was in night visions. The sense of \"the word of YHWH came to Abram in a vision\" is like the sense of \"and all the people saw the voices\" (Exodus 20:18), and their secret belongs to those who know grace:" "<b>Do not fear, Abram</b> — He was afraid of two things: of the kings, lest they multiply their armies against him — they or those who stand under them — and in battle he descend and be wiped out; or lest his day come to die without seed. And He promised him that He Himself would be a shield on his behalf against them, and furthermore that there would be reward for his walking with HaShem, very much indeed:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase לְיוֹדְעֵי חֵן (\"to those who know grace\") is a cryptic kabbalistic allusion; rendered literally and left unexplained per the voice rules."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:21.770382186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}